---
description: Require function parameters; only use ? and default args when they are actually optional.
globs: **/*.ts
alwaysApply: true
---

# Required parameters

Mark parameters optional (`?`) or give default arguments only when a caller is meant to omit them. If the value is always provided, type it as required and do not fall back with `??` / `||` at the call boundary.

```typescript
// ❌
export const generateBackendApp = async (args: {
  reader?: IDeterministicReader;
  settings?: GenerateContext["settings"];
}) =>
  generate({
    reader: args.reader ?? memoryReader({}),
    settings: args.settings ?? {},
  });

// ✅
export const generateBackendApp = async (args: {
  reader: IDeterministicReader;
  settings: GenerateContext["settings"];
}) =>
  generate({
    reader: args.reader,
    settings: args.settings,
  });
```

`section?: string` on a patch helper is fine: the section is genuinely optional.
